# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# GATE-HYGIENE: description strings must contain NO dollar-sign and NO backtick (set -u in the runner).
register_gate "tests/test_code_node_shape_persist.py" "CODE-NODE SHAPE PERSIST GATE: PASS" "code_node signature-shape persistence: the extractor's content-free def shape survives BOTH governed write paths" "code_node signature-shape persistence (compatibility lane PR-1): the content-free signature shape the Python extractor attaches to def nodes (parameter names, required and optional arity counts, varargs and kwargs flags, keyword-only names, a hash fingerprint) was silently DROPPED at ingest because the governed INSERT enumerated only id/kind/path/name/language/span/hash. This gate proves the fix end to end on a real database through the real SECURITY DEFINER write path, for BOTH paths: full ingest_graph persists the shape byte-equal to the extraction; patch_graph (the steady-state incremental path a normal push takes) persists it too, so a normal push can never wipe it; file and class rows store all seven columns NULL; no default-value token, annotation token, body token, or default literal appears anywhere in any stored row (whole-row superuser read); malformed shape fields (wrong types, out-of-bounds counts, oversized arrays, junk fingerprints) degrade to NULL without error and the sanitizer bound provably matches the schema CHECK bound. Content-free: names plus counts plus flags plus a hash only. Nothing reads the columns yet." "code_node signature-shape persistence holds on both governed write paths: shape stored byte-equal on full ingest and on the steady-state incremental patch; non-def rows all-NULL; no default/annotation/body bytes at the store; malformed fields degrade to NULL never abort; sanitizer bound equals schema bound. Gate 246." 20
